## Call chain

| Layer | Entry | Input | Output | Side effects |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| L1 | `FeeInclusivePnl.evaluate` | checked instrument, round trip, fee policies | typed fee-inclusive PnL or non-empty typed violations | none |
| L2 | `ScenarioValuation.pricePnl` | checked instrument and round trip | exact price PnL or scenario-native error | none |
| L3 | `AttributedPricePnl.calculate` | ordered attributed changes and flat endpoint | exact attributed price PnL or accumulated typed violations | none |

## Happy path

Valid single- and multi-slice long/short round trips retain exact price PnL, attribution order, settled fees, and net PnL. The scenario and fee-policy public-path suites passed unchanged.

## Critical error path

A same-instrument-ID market from a foreign reference-data lineage is rejected by `AttributedPricePnl.calculate`. `ScenarioValuation.pricePnl` maps the retained `ReferenceDataError` to `ScenarioValuationError.SliceValue` at the original exit leg and slice without fabricating an instrument mismatch. `FeeInclusivePnl.evaluate` retains that exact nested cause in `FeeInclusiveScenarioPriceFailure`.

